Encounter: Virizion

# Virizion, "The Graceful Blade". One rule, stated in both directions:
#   MOMENTUM IS VIRIZION'S ARMOUR. IT ONLY FLOWS WHILE ITS RHYTHM HOLDS - BREAK THE RHYTHM AND THE
#   ARMOUR GOES WITH IT.
#   MOMENTUM 0-5 (0-7 from Phase 1) IS the damage-reduction guard: EncScript_Virizion_ApplyFlow is
#   its only writer and Momentum is its only input, written absolutely - 78 at 0, 97 at 7, three
#   points a step. Unlike both siblings the phase does not own the guard; the meter does, so the
#   Momentum callout carries the whole of guideline 14.
#     +1  Virizion's side took health off you this turn
#     +1  ...and nothing took health off Virizion (a flawless pass)
#     +1  Virizion knocked one of your Pokemon out
#     +1  every turn, unconditionally, once SACRED BLADE begins
#     ->0 a turn Virizion's side took no health off you (Protect, a miss, a sleep turn, a resist)
#     ->0 a super-effective type landed on it
#     ->0 it is carrying a status at turn close
#     ->0 its Speed stage is below neutral at turn close
#   MOMENTUM buys Virizion evasion, not skin:
#     3+  BLADE DANCE - on a turn the meter rose, its blow carries into a second scripted slash;
#         plus +2 evasion, +1 Speed and a raised critical-hit ratio (encsetcrit)
#     5+  UNTOUCHABLE (Phase 1+) - a telegraphed scripted dodge on a 2-turn cooldown, plus +1 Speed
#     5   Phase 0's ceiling
#     7   Untouchable's ceiling, and in SACRED BLADE the point the charge fires
#   A break drops the meter to 0 and nothing more - that alone is 15-19 guard points and evasion,
#   crit and Speed stripped in one beat. The fight is about the turns AFTER you take the armour off.
# Phase 1 (50%) UNTOUCHABLE: raw Speed +10% written into the stats, the ceiling rises to 7, the
#   scripted dodges go live, Blade Dance hits harder, slot 3 becomes Close Combat, and Virizion now
#   SHEDS what slows it - a status is cleared at turn open and a lowered Speed stage climbs back one
#   a turn. Status and Speed control stop being locks and become a per-turn cost.
# Phase 2 (15%) SACRED BLADE: Momentum rises +1 EVERY turn regardless of whether Virizion landed
#   anything, so only a real disruptor stops the climb. At 7 it fires SACRED SWORD for 32% of your
#   side and falls back to 3. Break the charge instead and it is left EXHAUSTED: meter 0, -1
#   Def/Sp. Def, and it loses its next action. Survive: True carries the fight to 1 HP.
# ANTI-ABUSE IS DISPLACEMENT, NOT IMMUNITY (guideline 8). In Phase 0 a status or a Speed drop holds
#   the meter at 0 for as long as the player maintains it - a genuinely strong opening counterplay,
#   and meant to be. From 50% Virizion sheds both, so they keep working but cost a move every turn.
#   Sacred Sword (fixed slot) ignores defensive boosts and evasion; Toxic is flat and, being a
#   status, holds the meter down in Phase 0.
Properties:
    Level: LevelCap
    CatchRate: 0                # none; EncScript_Virizion_Spent sets a real one
    Balls: Blocked
    DamageReduction: 88         # Momentum 0. Every later value is written absolutely by
                                # EncScript_Virizion_ApplyFlow, which _Intro calls on turn 0
    Immunities: Ohko, FixedDamage, HpSwap, SharedKo
    CapTypeEffectiveness: True  # Grass/Fighting is 4x weak to FLYING - exactly the spike the cap
                                # exists to flatten, and Flying coverage is everywhere
    FlatToxicDamage: True
    Survive: True               # load-bearing: 1 HP is what ends SACRED BLADE and opens the catch
                                # window, and an oversized hit into a Momentum-0 guard of 78 could
                                # otherwise skip the whole last phase. Cleared in _Spent
    Ability: ABILITY_JUSTIFIED  # its own. A Dark move raises its Attack, so the obvious neutral
                                # coverage answer feeds it
    Moves: MOVE_SACRED_SWORD, MOVE_LEAF_BLADE, MOVE_QUICK_ATTACK, MOVE_MAGICAL_LEAF
    AiFlags: AI_FLAG_SMART_TRAINER

# Always-true block: pins the variable numbering the battle scripts hard-code. encounterproc assigns
# each Var() an index in first-appearance order, so naming all sixteen here in order fixes
# Phase..StepGuard to 0..15. No var-to-var comparison appears anywhere in this design; every test is
# against a literal, the two ceilings (5 and 7) are reached by branching on Phase first, and
# ENC_SNAP_DAMAGE is the engine's own answer to "subtract one value from another".
# 0 Phase (0 The Graceful Blade / 1 Untouchable / 2 Sacred Blade / 3 Spent),
# 1 Momentum (0-5, or 0-7 from Phase 1), 2 LastMom (the last ANNOUNCED Momentum - the callout's
# re-fire latch), 3 Tier (which Momentum perks are applied: 0 none / 1 the 3+ set / 2 the 5+ set),
# 4 TurnGuard (the once-per-turn scaffold), 5 Landed (Virizion's side took HP off the player this
# turn), 6 Broke (a break already fired this turn - the de-duplicator), 7 Rose (the meter rose this
# turn - Blade Dance's gate), 8 Danced (Blade Dance already fired this turn), 9 PlayerMark (player
# HP% at turn open; ENC_SNAP_DAMAGE turns it into "lost this turn"), 10 BossMark (Virizion HP% at
# turn open; likewise), 11 Scratch (the copy ENC_SNAP_DAMAGE consumes, so a mark survives being
# measured against), 12 DodgeCd (turns until the scripted dodge may fire again), 13 EventGuard
# (per-turn guard shared by OnSwitchIn and OnFaint, so a forced replacement is not double-counted),
# 14 Ultimate (how many Sacred Swords have fired - drives the escalating line),
# 15 StepGuard (per-turn guard for _Footing's one-stage Speed recovery, so it does not re-select
# inside one checkpoint's re-evaluation loop while Speed is still below neutral).
Trigger: OnBattleStart
Priority: 10
Flags: Once
Script: EncScript_Virizion_Intro
Conditions:
    Var(Phase) >= 0
    Var(Momentum) >= 0
    Var(LastMom) >= 0
    Var(Tier) >= 0
    Var(TurnGuard) >= 0
    Var(Landed) >= 0
    Var(Broke) >= 0
    Var(Rose) >= 0
    Var(Danced) >= 0
    Var(PlayerMark) >= 0
    Var(BossMark) >= 0
    Var(Scratch) >= 0
    Var(DodgeCd) >= 0
    Var(EventGuard) >= 0
    Var(Ultimate) >= 0
    Var(StepGuard) >= 0

# The three phase transitions. Each is registered at both checkpoints because the blow that crosses
# a threshold can be a move or an end-of-turn tick; both copies are Once, which is marked at
# SELECTION, so whichever fires first permanently disables the other. All three sit below _TurnClose
# (80), so at an OnTurnEnd where the player's damage crossed a threshold the transition runs first
# and everything after it sees the new Phase. Same shape as Dialga, Palkia and both siblings.
Trigger: OnMoveEnd
Priority: 5
Flags: Once, OnEnter
Script: EncScript_Virizion_Untouchable
Conditions:
    Battler(Boss).HpPercent <= 50
    Var(Phase) == 0

Trigger: OnTurnEnd
Priority: 5
Flags: Once, OnEnter
Script: EncScript_Virizion_Untouchable
Conditions:
    Battler(Boss).HpPercent <= 50
    Var(Phase) == 0

Trigger: OnMoveEnd
Priority: 6
Flags: Once, OnEnter
Script: EncScript_Virizion_SacredBlade
Conditions:
    Battler(Boss).HpPercent <= 15
    Var(Phase) == 1

Trigger: OnTurnEnd
Priority: 6
Flags: Once, OnEnter
Script: EncScript_Virizion_SacredBlade
Conditions:
    Battler(Boss).HpPercent <= 15
    Var(Phase) == 1

Trigger: OnMoveEnd
Priority: 7
Flags: Once
Script: EncScript_Virizion_Spent
Conditions:
    Battler(Boss).HpPercent <= 1
    Var(Phase) == 2

Trigger: OnTurnEnd
Priority: 7
Flags: Once
Script: EncScript_Virizion_Spent
Conditions:
    Battler(Boss).HpPercent <= 1
    Var(Phase) == 2

# The once-per-turn scaffold. Ticks the dodge cooldown, snapshots the two HP marks the turn is
# measured against, runs the recurring flow line, and clears the per-turn state. TurnGuard is set
# immediately so no branch out of the script can leave it re-armed.
Trigger: OnTurnStart
Priority: 10
Script: EncScript_Virizion_TurnOpen
Conditions:
    Var(TurnGuard) == 0

# The anti-abuse pair, Phase 1+ only. Priority above _TurnOpen (10) so they see the per-turn state
# it just reset. In Phase 0 neither exists: a status and a Speed drop stick and hold the meter at 0.
Trigger: OnTurnStart
Priority: 12
Script: EncScript_Virizion_Shed
Conditions:
    Var(Phase) >= 1
    Var(Phase) <= 2
    Battler(Boss).Status >= 1

Trigger: OnTurnStart
Priority: 13
Script: EncScript_Virizion_Footing
Conditions:
    Var(Phase) >= 1
    Var(Phase) <= 2
    Var(StepGuard) == 0
    Battler(Boss).Stat(STAT_SPEED) < DEFAULT_STAT_STAGE

# The telegraphed dodge. Announced before the player's move resolves, so the turn can be spent on
# setup, a heal or a switch instead. Set at OnTurnStart it covers the whole turn and expires on its
# own; the 2-turn cooldown is DodgeCd, decremented in _TurnOpen.
Trigger: OnTurnStart
Priority: 15
Script: EncScript_Virizion_Dodge
Conditions:
    Var(Phase) >= 1
    Var(Phase) <= 2
    Var(Momentum) >= 5
    Var(DodgeCd) == 0

# THE BREAK-BY-TYPE trigger. A Flying / Fire / Ice / Poison / Psychic / Fairy move landed on
# Virizion - exactly Grass/Fighting's weaknesses, so "a super-effective type landed on it" is
# expressible without an effectiveness operand. At OnMoveEnd Event.Battler is the battler that GOT
# HIT. Self-disables through Broke, which _Break sets; nesting depth 2, well inside the limit of 4.
Trigger: OnMoveEnd
Priority: 30
Script: EncScript_Virizion_BreakType
Conditions:
    Var(Broke) == 0
    Var(TurnGuard) == 1
    Var(Phase) <= 2
    Var(Momentum) >= 1
    Event.Battler == B_POSITION_OPPONENT_LEFT
    Any:
        Event.MoveType == TYPE_FLYING
        Event.MoveType == TYPE_FIRE
        Event.MoveType == TYPE_ICE
        Event.MoveType == TYPE_POISON
        Event.MoveType == TYPE_PSYCHIC
        Event.MoveType == TYPE_FAIRY

# A player Pokemon went down. EventGuard stops the replacement switch-in being processed a second
# time; the +1 is applied by _TheyFell.
Trigger: OnFaint
Priority: 30
Script: EncScript_Virizion_TheyFell
Conditions:
    Var(EventGuard) == 0
    Var(Phase) <= 2
    Event.Battler == B_POSITION_PLAYER_LEFT

# TurnGuard == 1 is load-bearing: OnSwitchIn fires for the player's lead BEFORE OnBattleStart, when
# every var is 0. Sets EventGuard and nothing else - a mid-turn switch (U-turn, Eject Button) only
# exists here so a faint later in the same turn is not double-counted.
Trigger: OnSwitchIn
Priority: 31
Script: EncScript_Virizion_TheyEntered
Conditions:
    Var(EventGuard) == 0
    Var(TurnGuard) == 1
    Var(Phase) <= 2
    Event.Battler == B_POSITION_PLAYER_LEFT

# THE LEDGER. Runs last of the OnTurnEnd measuring scripts that read HP, so it sees a finished turn:
# the master rule (Virizion's side took no health off you -> break), the flawless-pass bonus, the
# Sacred Blade auto-climb, the guard restored absolutely, and the callout. Self-disables by clearing
# TurnGuard.
Trigger: OnTurnEnd
Priority: 80
Script: EncScript_Virizion_TurnClose
Conditions:
    Var(TurnGuard) == 1

# _Slowed (82) and _Statused (83) run AFTER _TurnClose (80) deliberately: _TurnClose raises the
# meter, then these two take it away in the same checkpoint, so a player holding Virizion slowed
# sees the meter tick up and immediately collapse. The Broke == 0 gate is what self-disables them -
# _Break sets Broke, and it also covers "a break already fired this turn" (the master rule, or a
# super-effective hit at OnMoveEnd), so at most one of the three break paths spends a turn.
Trigger: OnTurnEnd
Priority: 82
Script: EncScript_Virizion_Slowed
Conditions:
    Var(Phase) <= 2
    Var(Broke) == 0
    Var(Momentum) >= 1
    Battler(Boss).Stat(STAT_SPEED) < DEFAULT_STAT_STAGE

Trigger: OnTurnEnd
Priority: 83
Script: EncScript_Virizion_Statused
Conditions:
    Var(Phase) <= 2
    Var(Broke) == 0
    Var(Momentum) >= 1
    Battler(Boss).Status >= 1

# BLADE DANCE's second slash. Runs after both disruptor triggers, so a meter that rose and was then
# broken does not also get to dance. Gated on Rose, so it only follows a turn the meter moved.
Trigger: OnTurnEnd
Priority: 85
Script: EncScript_Virizion_Dance
Conditions:
    Var(Phase) <= 2
    Var(Momentum) >= 3
    Var(Rose) == 1
    Var(Danced) == 0

# SACRED SWORD. Runs AFTER _TurnClose (80), which is what pushes Momentum to 7 in SACRED BLADE; it
# is selected on the re-evaluation pass that follows (determinism rule 3), exactly like Terrakion's
# Collapse. Self-disables by resetting Momentum to 3.
Trigger: OnTurnEnd
Priority: 91
Script: EncScript_Virizion_SacredSword
Conditions:
    Var(Phase) == 2
    Var(Momentum) >= 7
